{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/751126-creating-from-scratch-powergamers-assemble","id":751126,"title":"Creating from scratch (powergamers assemble!)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-03T04:35:35-08:00","id":751126,"title":"Creating from scratch (powergamers assemble!)","content":"EDIT: NECROED thread, please, read last post.<br /> <br /> We all know that for creating things from scratch requires Prime 2. But what if you don't have Prime 2 and you want to &quot;create&quot; something?<br /> Well, I'm creating this thread and calling all creative powergamers to help and post ways to get around this.<br /> I know that every paradigm/practice would use different ways of doing it, but I am interested in rules only.<br /> So, if your Mage wants to create a fireball independent if the situation/environment, what do you do?<br /> Don't mind about vulgarity!<br /> <br /> -Forces: As we know, Forces 3 can transform and amplify anything related to Forces. So you could just transform the light of the environment or the gravity in an area if its a dark area. Now if you are in a dark and quiet room in space (no gravity) I'm out of ideas. Anyone?<br /> <br /> -Mind: The mage could use his own emotions, thoughts or synapses to fuel his spell. Maybe spending a Quintessence point to help increase the mental processes that will fuel the transformation. This could be done regardless of the environment <br /> <br /> -Matter: Not so many options with this one. The only way I can think is transforming any kind of object into energy. Einstein already showed to us that matter is indeed equal to energy in a way. So, your Mage could just carry some little objects and uae them as fuel.<br /> <br /> -Life: As The Matrix already said, the human body is a living battery. The mage could transform his body energy/heat or muscular energy into Forces energy to fuel his spells. Would also say that it requires one Quintessence point to increase body energy to such a great level. Also independent of the environment.<br /> As with Matter, I believe that Life could transform the life energy of a living being into Forces energy. Maybe the mage could even use the microorganisms of the environment to fuel his spell. Altought this would depend on the environment, it wouldn't require a Quintessence point.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Couldn't think of a way of doing with Spirit and I believe that Correspondence, Time and Entropy are useless here. But I would be glad to be wrong.<br /> <br /> All the examples would require lvl 3 on the spheres probably.<br /> <br /> That's it. I'm very excited to see other ideas. And please, PLEASE, don't post things like &quot;this is not the way Mage should be played&quot; or &quot;stop powergaming&quot; =)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","user":"Lord Revan","date":". 03-24-2022, 10:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T05:19:15-08:00","id":751189,"title":"","content":"Transforming Life or Matter patterns into Engery takes conjunctional Forces 3. Going by how do you do that changing objects into potentially explosive substances also takes conjunctional forces (which is stupid but well you want RAW).<br /> <br /> Corr 4 opens a portal to the sun. Less a fireball and more of a vulgar fuck you spell that will incinerate yourself aswell (or at least cause a fuckton of paradox).<br /> Time 5 can open a temporal gateway to the past when the world was still young and not yet cooled off. Also vulgar and very hard to pull off. Time 5 forces 3 could potentially transmute time into a fireball - but I don't even know what consequences that would have (same for corr 5 and space I guess).<br /> Entropy 6 can cause spontaneaus fire, Entropy 3 can set someone aflame if there is a reasonable way it could have happened without magic (running into a fuel canister while smoking).<br /> <br /> Spirit 2 call a fire spirit.<br /> <br /> In general if you use Forces 3+ to transmute something into a force it will usually cause some sort of (often unpleasant) unbalance. Transmuting gravity into fire (aside from being very vulgar) can screw up gravity in that area for some time. Transmuting your emotions may cause you to loose willpower or cause derangements, Life may cause damage or genetic flaws etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T05:45:13-08:00","id":751203,"title":"","content":"Forces 3/Life 3 - transmute the sound of traffic into a large number of giant clams and drop them on your opponents.<br /> <br /> You used to be able to do this with giant squid, but it's not clear if M20 classes squid as simple or complex life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T06:38:19-08:00","id":751279,"title":"","content":"Good replies. Yes, in my examples I was always considering conjunctional effect with Forces 3, since it is a fireball example.<br /> <br /> Flinty, hadn't thought about portals, that's very good. And the mage could even &quot;aim&quot; The portal to his target. Time, Correspondence and Entropy are very hard to help in a spell like this and probably would require a lot of successes.<br /> <br /> About the Life and Mind consequences, I thought about it and that's why I imagined that a Quintessence point would help to empower the mage thoughts/body so the spell wouldn't harm him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T09:28:27-08:00","id":751578,"title":"","content":"At least as far as Mind-Forces goes, I think that I remember reading in &quot;How Do You DO That?&quot; that it requires additional expenditures. Extreme concentration and transmutations of mental energy into actual Forces should require the expenditure of a Willpower point. (Actually, after looking this up, the text actually says that a ST is well within their rights to require a point of Willpower. It also goes on to describe the Effect as Mind3/Forces3/Prime2, but I think that it's actually describing the Effect as using mental powers to conjure flame, not necessarily transmuting mental energies.)<br /> <br /> I'd rule something similar for transmuting Life energies into Forces, by ruling that it's either limited by your Stamina (over a given time period, probably a day), or that you take levels of bashing damage for Effect cast this way. Maybe even both, taking bashing damage for every Effect past your dots in Stamina.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6384-frozenfishy","name":"Frozenfishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T09:56:37-08:00","id":751604,"title":"","content":"Frozenfishy, you're right. The example in HDYDT is about a psychic mage conjuring things from nothing. That's why they listed Prime 2.<br /> In my case the intention isn't creating from nothing, but from other sources that different spheres than Prime could provide.<br /> I could see a Mind conjunctional spell spend willpower instead of Quintessence too.<br /> <br /> About the Life example, I also can see a health lvl. But as even Prime 1 proves, a health level equals 1 Quintessence point, so maybe this could be done, expend 1 Quint instead of taking damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","user":"Lord Revan","date":". 11-03-2015, 12:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T11:04:17-08:00","id":751754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/751126-creating-from-scratch-powergamers-assemble?p=751604#post751604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> About the Life example, I also can see a health lvl. But as even Prime 1 proves, a health level equals 1 Quintessence point, so maybe this could be done, expend 1 Quint instead of taking damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something like this could indeed be done, by using conjunctional prime at level ~3. Kinda defeats the purpose here.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T20:16:44-08:00","id":752872,"title":"","content":"You don't have to be a powergamer to want to figure out different ways to use the magic rules independent of paradigm. It's true that systems and paradigms work together to a degree, but sometimes you get more clarity from looking at them separately. There are a lot of people who care a lot about roleplaying but also have a compulsively thorough approach to systems. I happen to be one of them. The better I understand the rules the better I can put them in the back of my mind and focus on roleplaying and storytelling. I'm sorry if you've been swarmed by in the past for asking questions like this. I'd be surprised if that has happened here, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","user":"Faradn","date":". 11-04-2015, 05:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T03:09:18-08:00","id":753506,"title":"","content":"Faradn, I also think this way. Even trying to get environment free ways to create from scratch.<br /> But some people might think that this is &quot;cheating&quot; and if I want to do that should get Prime 2, I don't know..<br /> <br /> Just ask help for completely avoid paradox and see what happens","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T04:03:31-08:00","id":753631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/751126-creating-from-scratch-powergamers-assemble?p=753506#post753506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just ask help for completely avoid paradox and see what happens</div> </div> </div> </div>On that topic, you're standing right here, and the point is somewhere near Timbuktu.<br /> <br /> To be a bit more helpful, your interpretations are all valid. Best of all they work both ways. You don't need to make forces from matter... you can make matter from forces, or emotions from life!<br /> <br /> Forces is self-explanatory. You should be able to transform Matter into Forces at Matter 2, Life will require you to use Life 4 (possibly 3 for simpler life forms) and will hurt/kill whatever you siphon from.<br /> <br /> Mind is a bit trickier, mostly because one person does not have enough emotion in him to actually create something, I would suggest taking a mass of people, that should be quite more productive - for instance siphoning the road rage of a whole freeway to create a horrifying conflagration that burns everything. You could even add Correspondance and siphon emotion or even memories of whole cities or countries to power an effect.<br /> <br /> Spirit won't help you much unless there is a materialised spirit or a fetish nearby to rip into something, but in the Umbra you could pretty much substitute Spirit 2/3 for Prime 2 to create anything you could possibly imagine.<br /> <br /> At Correspondance 5 you can colocate and destroy space, you could actually destroy space and turn it into something else at that point. I'm not sure it's something you would want to do, though.<br /> <br /> Entropy can cause effects you want it to in a roundabout way. It doesn't deal with anything that you can exactly turn into something else, but I would postulate that if you can find Oblivion or a realm that is reflection of the Wyrm, you could use Entropy 4/5 (possibly with Spirit) to change that into anything you might need. The Resonance would be murder, though.<br /> <br /> Time. Well. If comic books have thought us anything it's that you CAN DESTROOOOY TIIIIIIME! Doing something like that would be horrifyingly vulgar and ineffiecient, but I can see a Marauder or Mad Scientist doing something like that with Time 5 (probably 6 since we're really going into narrative effects). Consequences of this lead to causality and history breaking to bits, do not mix with alcohol and medications and consult your storyteller before attempting to break the setting into tiny pieces of confetti.<br /> <br /> This leads us back into Prime - all these things can be turned into primal energies that could shape infinite works or into quintessence that could be used or stored as Tass.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T05:24:12-08:00","id":753758,"title":"","content":"There were threads about paradox handling with requests not only made by me, that eventually got some people mad. But nevermind this.<br /> <br /> Cogliostro, very nice!<br /> As we can see the non pattern spheres are way dificult to help here, always involving long rituals just to cast a simple fireball from &quot;nothing&quot;.<br /> <br /> The purpose of the thread is to find ways to create stuff (Forces, Matter, Life) from nothing anywhere! Which means being capable to create stuff from nothing even in extreme situations, like lost in a desert, locked into a dark empty room, or even in space, where you will not have almost anything to transform.<br /> And I would say that the best spheres to do that are Forces and Life.<br /> I still don't know how Forces could be transformed in an environment without gravity, light or sound.<br /> This makes me believe that Life is the winner sphere here, because even that the mage find himself in a place without any kind of life, even the microscopic ones, he himself is a living being. So he could harness his own life energy anywhere, at the cost of health levels or Quintessence.<br /> <br /> Thanks for all good replies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T10:26:15-08:00","id":754409,"title":"","content":"Paradigm shouldn't be ignored when it comes to something like this. If you have a Forces Mage who made it through high school physics, then you have someone who probably believes in atoms and molecules. So even if he's stuck in a place without gravity, light or sound, he may still be able to influence the forces that bond atoms and molecules together. Covalent bonds, and such. If I were the storyteller, I'd make it very difficult to do, mind you. But it would be possible, and probably pack quite an oomph if converted correctly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T10:43:30-08:00","id":754428,"title":"","content":"When I say to don't mind paradigm it means that I want to know if it's possible rule wise, not in game. Of course the mage would still need to fit the effect into his paradigm later in game.<br /> <br /> Good idea, altough messing with atoms (from the atmosphere/oxygen I believe, that exists in an empty room) would probably require Matter too, am I right?<br /> <br /> PS: what oomph means?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T11:02:54-08:00","id":754544,"title":"","content":"In this context, &quot;oomph&quot; means power and impact. Atomic forces are scary.<br /> <br /> If you're manipulating the atoms themselves, you'd need matter. But if you're manipulating the forces and interaction between the atoms, such as the covalent bonds which hold electrons together, that'd be forces. <br /> <br /> I think you can't completely divorce paradigm and rule because sometimes paradigm can influence the kinds of forces/matter/life materials you have at your disposal. Especially when you start getting into things that can't be easily observed like Quarks, electrons, ether or dark matter. If you don't believe in it, you can't use it...if you do...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T11:29:11-08:00","id":754596,"title":"","content":"Kalinara, I see. I have no idea how to rule such transformation, but it absolutely is useful!<br /> <br /> Yeah, when you post something about atoms consider that the mage believes in atoms and when you post something about gods consider that he believes in gods. It's simple =)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T11:39:58-08:00","id":754609,"title":"","content":"I think that messing with atomic bonds and charges was the purview of Forces 5. I'm pretty sure that you could use that to do insane tricks with Forces, up to and including nuclear fission.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T17:08:01-08:00","id":755279,"title":"","content":"Isn't Forces able to manipulate Darkness, too?. I'm sure than in revised that was true, but I don't know if M20 retconned this.<br /> <br /> If Forces can also manipulate &quot;negative forces&quot; (darkness, cold, silence), then you're never truly out of Forces to transmute.<br /> <br /> Also Matter it's pretty damn common in the material plane. While nearly useless in the Umbra (replace with Spirit), you will always have SOME Matter to transmute (like the air, or the ground).<br /> <br /> There's nothing bad/munchkin about theorizing about the rules. I love to do it. Munchkin may be the intent (and, let's be honest, as far as powergaming goes, this it's very minor).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T17:54:55-08:00","id":755403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/751126-creating-from-scratch-powergamers-assemble?p=755279#post755279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't Forces able to manipulate Darkness, too?. I'm sure than in revised that was true, but I don't know if M20 retconned this.<br /> <br /> If Forces can also manipulate &quot;negative forces&quot; (darkness, cold, silence), then you're never truly out of Forces to transmute.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's true, I remember reading that too. However, it does run up against balance issues and will give a Storyteller a bit of a hard time to deal with it. For example, if you transmute darkness into Matter, what rushes in to fill the void left behind? After all, the entire space that the darkness previously occupied can't <i>entirely </i>be the new Matter. Like going the other direction, or even sticking within the realm of Forces, it should take a <i>ton</i> of light to transmute into any kind of damaging amount of energy, like a fireball or a beam.<br /> <br /> Really the best way to deal with &quot;manipulating Darkness&quot; is the negative, or rather the positive. Manipulate the light that defines the shadows. <br /> <br /> I know that this is a topic about powergaming, but I thought I'd inject a little tempering reason...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6384-frozenfishy","name":"Frozenfishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T23:10:10-08:00","id":755926,"title":"","content":"I was thinking about transforming darkness, but what would be the side effect? It can't be light, so I believe that would be less darkness?<br /> And I think that Forces manipulate darkness by controling light, not darkness itself since darkness is merely the absence of light.<br /> <br /> Frozenfishy, remember that Forces can amplify its sources, so you can create a big fireball out of pratically very small Forces, as long as you have sufficient successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T00:51:28-08:00","id":755963,"title":"","content":"Darkness in Mage is not &quot;absence of light&quot;, it's shadows and murky evil darkness that envelops all. Forces doesn't work according to any sensible laws of physics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T03:00:28-08:00","id":756107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/751126-creating-from-scratch-powergamers-assemble?p=755963#post755963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Darkness in Mage is not &amp;quot;absence of light&amp;quot;, it's shadows and murky evil darkness that envelops all. Forces doesn't work according to any sensible laws of physics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. I remember Mage rev description of Forces talking about something like that. But I don't know what would be the consequences of transforming darkness into energy, less darkness?<br /> <br /> Maybe something similar could be made with temperature, transforming the heat energy of the environment into energy. Unless you are in a 0\u00b0K (-273\u00b0C,-459\u00b0F) there are heat and molecular agitation ready to be used anywhere in the universe!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T11:38:29-08:00","id":761633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/751126-creating-from-scratch-powergamers-assemble?p=755963#post755963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Darkness in Mage is not &quot;absence of light&quot;, it's shadows and murky evil darkness that envelops all. Forces doesn't work according to any sensible laws of physics.</div> </div> </div> </div>More accurately, Darkness is not &quot;absence of Light&quot; in non-Technoparadigm.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> A whole lot of these ideas for &quot;creating from scratch&quot;, including all the ones in the OP, are easily compressible into a single, core thing: <i>turn Pattern X into different Pattern Y</i>. In other words, as long as you have some <i>thing</i> you're willing to use as 'raw materials', you can make something else with it, as long as you have the ruling Spheres for both the source item and the result item.<br /> <br /> Typically the Patterning Spheres are Life, Forces, or Matter, but Mind and Spirit also act as Pattern Spheres for their respective abstracted phenomena (mental constructs and spiritual manifestations). You might even be able to use the glow of your own anima as a source for physical light or other energy (a Spirit 2/Forces 3 rote) similar to an Exalt's Anima Banner.<br /> <br /> There might even be Patterns ruled by Correspondence and Time which can be sacrificed, and one could conceivably cause something to come into being by corroding organizational structures with Entropy, if you get esoteric enough.<br /> <br /> Transmuting to and from Prime, of course, is the straightforward &quot;make something from nothing&quot; and &quot;destroy a Pattern&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T16:43:42-08:00","id":761831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/751126-creating-from-scratch-powergamers-assemble?p=761633#post761633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You might even be able to use the glow of your own anima as a source for physical light or other energy (a Spirit 2/Forces 3 rote) similar to an Exalt's Anima Banner.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not entirely comfortable with that idea. Even with using Mind or Life as raw material for transmutations, I'd stipulate that you're using un(magickally)healing damage for Life and Willpower points for Mind. If you aren't using Prime, the most prescribed method for ex nihilo creation, then it needs to cost something. If you're transmuting your aura, what could that cost?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6384-frozenfishy","name":"Frozenfishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T17:03:56-08:00","id":761845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frozenfishy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/751126-creating-from-scratch-powergamers-assemble?p=761831#post761831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not entirely comfortable with that idea. Even with using Mind or Life as raw material for transmutations, I'd stipulate that you're using un(magickally)healing damage for Life and Willpower points for Mind. If you aren't using Prime, the most prescribed method for ex nihilo creation, then it needs to cost something. If you're transmuting your aura, what could that cost?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Fair enough. As I said, I would rule that you could spend a Quintessence point instead to increase your body/mind energy to avoid those consequences. It could be used for the auar as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T19:54:26-08:00","id":761955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frozenfishy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/751126-creating-from-scratch-powergamers-assemble?p=761831#post761831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not entirely comfortable with that idea. Even with using Mind or Life as raw material for transmutations, I'd stipulate that you're using un(magickally)healing damage for Life and Willpower points for Mind. If you aren't using Prime, the most prescribed method for ex nihilo creation, then it needs to cost something. If you're transmuting your aura, what could that cost?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I imagine that making the 'glow' of your soul show up as physical light wouldn't be that big a deal; you're effectively just shifting it from being visible in the Umbra to being visible in reality.<br /> <br /> I vaguely recall there being <i>somewhere</i> in an earlier edition that gave Spirit 2 alongside Prime 2 as a way of conjuring things from apparent nowhere. Can't seem to find it though.<br /> <br /> You might also be able to spend Soul Points (which are otherwise only canonically used for fueling Infernal Investments) if you're really desperate or willing to dig that deep. Oddly, losing bits of your soul doesn't seem to actually <i>do</i> anything, though who knows what effect slowly cutting away your humanity would have regarding Disembodiment...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6072,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","user":"Quantumboost","date":". 11-09-2015, 10:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T19:42:07-07:00","id":1477298,"title":"","content":"I'm necroeing (?) this thread to get more ideas on how to do that with Forces 3 only.<br /> <br /> So, curse of friction is a rote that let's a Forces 3 mage transform the target movement into heat, making it imobile and dealing damage. It also can turn the target breath into freezing cold, enough to hold him in a block of ice. This shows just how much Forces 3 can indeed increase the energy that is being manipulated.<br /> Another example of energy increase is ik hdydt, where Forces 3 is able to lift about 2 tons just by manipulating forces.<br /> <br /> Having said that, I ask you: what are the best options of energies to transform? The more abundant and strong the energy is the better. Gravity and magnetism are practically constant on Earth snd pretty strong. Electromagnetic waves are also present almost anywhere. So there are a lot of options.<br /> <br /> However, in a very specific and scarce scenario, like for example in deep space, there wouldn't be Earth's magnetic field nor magnetic field. Electromagnetic waves would probably be present, otherwise the mage won't be able to even see. And thermal energy is definitely present. Otherwise...well... The mage would already be dead in the 2,7 K almost absolute 0 temperature of intergalactic space.<br /> <br /> Now, all this have consequences. Transforming a kind of energy into another will make the original kind to disappear. This means that transforming gravity into lightning would make things weightless, transforming light would make the area dark and transforming heat would make the area cold. I don't know if this would have a mechanical consequence, though. It would also last for a fraction of a second, which is the time the electric arc would take to hit the target, so maybe that's no big deal?<br /> <br /> So, what you guys think? What you believe it's the best option? And if there is any other that's worth mentioning, please do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T04:09:17-07:00","id":1477431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/751126-creating-from-scratch-powergamers-assemble?p=1477298#post1477298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm necroeing (?) this thread to get more ideas on how to do that with Forces 3 only.<br /> Having said that, I ask you: what are the best options of energies to transform? The more abundant and strong the energy is the better. Gravity and magnetism are practically constant on Earth snd pretty strong. Electromagnetic waves are also present almost anywhere. So there are a lot of options.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Earlier in the thread you said something along the lines of 'paradigm doesn't matter' but you're using a technocratic, science based paradigm here which makes me think that you're making the classic mistake of Mage players/STs in thinking that the player reality science is pretty much the same as the game's consensual reality.<br /> <br /> i.e. you're assuming that consensual reality's rules are science based when they're not. The consensual reality rules are based on spheres - they are in fact the game rules and the game makes a strong point that the paradigm a mage believes in is what really matters.<br /> <br /> This is something that a lot of powergamers have trouble with in Mage, they try to use 'science' to blag their way through a spell effect even when thy are using a non-science paradigm. The funny thing is there are plenty of options to powergame spells - try looking at the 'pulling on mythic treads' rules for a start.<br /> <br /> To answer your question it _is_ important to know the paradigm as that is what allows you to manipulate reality, most of the previous answers approach it from a technocratic science point of view so I'll try something different.<br /> <br /> A couple of points - Firstly, converting invisible forces into visible forces is something that I personally wouldn't allow as there's a good reason why Prime 2 is required, which is to stop blaggards powergaming everything! Furthermore with Forces 3 you can only transmute minor forces in limited areas, M20 p516 lists things that can be transmuted if you combine other spheres so all of those are out of bounds, meaning we are looking at pure force to pure force. Lastly, this is always vulgar and depends on getting a large number of successes on an Arete roll which means it requires a pretty powerful mage or some serious preparation. You should also be prepared for high levels of paradox.<br /> <br /> Given all those restrictions the only thing I can think of that even comes close is Aether (<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aether_(classical_element)\" target=\"_blank\">Aether (classical element) - Wikipedia</a>) - the Sons of Ether posit that everywhere is full of 'ether' which can be used to power their spells, if your ST is willing to let you blag it without Prime 2 then you could use Forces 3 to transmute the ether into whatever you want.<br /> <br /> In a similar vein there are a couple of other aether-like energies although they require quite an extreme paradigm that is laden with vulgar magic and paradox<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vril\" target=\"_blank\">Vril - Wikipedia</a><br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orgone\" target=\"_blank\">Orgone - Wikipedia</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T18:26:51-07:00","id":1477498,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11490_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11490\" data-vbnamecard=\"11490\">Dogstar</a> thank you for your answer.<br /> <br /> First, there are a few things that I want to adress.<br /> A) This is a necroed thread. The OP eas made in 2015 and I indeed wasn't looking for paradigm dependant examples, and tried to get examples using all spheres. Now I'm just trying to get pure Forces 3 examples and with a scientific paradigm.<br /> <br /> B) The vulgarity and paradox of an effect, except in very special cases, doesn't change according to the effect being much or less vulgar. Vulgar is vulgar and it will generate 1 paradox (in M20) unless botched.<br /> <br /> C) Paradigm do affect magick, but there is a limit. You can't just believe there is an infinite all powerfull energy that he taps just by breathing and then get free fuel for spells. Your examples of Aether, orgone, etc. looks like quintessence. I'd say that to tap into that you need Prime 2. I'm not sure paradigm can affect hsme mechanics that much.<br /> <br /> Also, there are only minor Forces involved. Forces 4 affects larger areas (miles, etc). The effect I'm proposing is definitely under Forces 3. And I don't get your visible/invisible argument, could you explain please?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}